    // Optimized fast-doubling algorithm for low-latency HLS synthesis.
    // This version computes F(n) for n>=0 with the following convention:
    // F(0)=0, F(1)=1, F(2)=1, F(3)=2, F(4)=3, F(5)=5, etc.
    // Use the iterative fast-doubling method, iterating over the bits
    // of n excluding the most-significant one. This guarantees that for
    // n=4 the function returns 3 and for n=5 it returns 5.
    //
    // Optimization: The loop is pipelined with an initiation interval of 1.
    
